<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Belgae (Britain)</h1><p class="st-meta">50 BCE – 43 CE (approx.) · capital Venta Belgarum (Winchester)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Central southern British people around Winchester, whose name recalls the Belgae of northern Gaul and who formed a civitas of Roman Britain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Caesar</a> wrote that the coastal parts of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> had been settled by Belgae from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> who kept their tribal names, and Belgic coins circulated widely in the south from the 2nd century BCE. A people called Belgae is named only from Roman times, however, and their pre-conquest identity is uncertain; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a>, the later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venta-belgarum">Venta Belgarum</a>, had a late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> enclosure at Oram's Arbour.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Before the conquest the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hampshire">Hampshire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiltshire">Wiltshire</a> seems to have fallen within the sphere of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/atrebates-britain">Atrebates (Britain)</a> and their kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commius">Commius</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tincomarus">Tincomarus</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verica">Verica</a>, sharing their coinage and links with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>. Farming was rich on the chalk downs, and hillforts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danebury">Danebury</a> had been major storage centres in earlier centuries.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 43 the area may first have been part of the realm of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/togidubnus">Togidubnus</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-regni">Kingdom of the Regni</a>. On his death it was organised as the civitas of the Belgae, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venta-belgarum">Venta Belgarum</a> as its capital; Ptolemy also lists <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bath">Aquae Sulis</a>, Bath, among their towns. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winchester">Winchester</a> later became the royal seat of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-wessex">Wessex</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 50 BCE – 43 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:58.71%;width:1.85%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>50 BCE – 43 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Venta Belgarum (Winchester)</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Common Brittonic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Belgae</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-4&amp;focus=belgae-britain" aria-label="Belgae (Britain) on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4650 407 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Belgae (Britain) lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4970 663L5304 942M4970 663L5020 640"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5304 942h0M5020 640h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4970 663h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4970 663h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Venta Belgarum. <a href="/atlas?year=-4&amp;focus=belgae-britain">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
